ce-roadmap-general-zlevels-name = Multi-Level
ce-roadmap-general-zlevels-desc = Stairs leading to roofs, pits leading to the abyss. Vertical gameplay that Space Station 14 sorely lacks.

ce-roadmap-general-ambitions-name = Ambitions
ce-roadmap-general-ambitions-desc = The ability to choose multiple procedurally generated roleplay tasks tied to existing players, items, and events in the current round.

ce-roadmap-guard-hard-labor-name = Hard Labor
ce-roadmap-guard-hard-labor-desc = Instead of jail cells and depriving the player of gameplay, guilty citizens will be sent to work off their debts to society through various menial labor under guard supervision... And will have the opportunity to escape.

ce-roadmap-farming-basic-farming-name = Basic Farming
ce-roadmap-farming-basic-farming-desc = Growing and harvesting plants, vegetables, fruits, and mushrooms at a basic level.

ce-roadmap-engineering-machine-construction-name = Machine Construction
ce-roadmap-engineering-machine-construction-desc = Using brass and iron, create various devices, from machine drills to trading platforms. Multi-stage assembly, disassembly, destruction, and repair of mechanisms.

ce-roadmap-engineering-powernet-name = Energy Crystals
ce-roadmap-engineering-powernet-desc = Arcane energy stored in every living being and concentrated in the world as energy crystals. Both useful and extremely dangerous. Use them as batteries for tools, run brass insulating pipes to power entire buildings and factories, or use them as weapons against your enemies.

ce-roadmap-engineering-air-crystals-name = Air Crystals
ce-roadmap-engineering-air-crystals-desc = A type of crystal capable of affecting wind currents. A volatile island core, the ability to create air lifts and hover in the air around dense air generators.

ce-roadmap-farming-silvas-name = Growing Silvas
ce-roadmap-farming-silvas-desc = The ability to grow various plants and mushrooms on the heads of silvas. Different plant types can provide various special effects, especially when it comes to magical mutated plants.

ce-roadmap-farming-magic-mutations-name = Magic Plants
ce-roadmap-farming-magic-mutations-desc = The ability to mutate ordinary boring plants into something special. Modular mutations will make the number of unique plant combinations enormous! Kudzu-pumpkin taking over the island, living walking mushrooms, or anti-gravity cherries granting a flight effect... And much more.

ce-roadmap-general-fligths-name = Flight
ce-roadmap-general-fligths-desc = The ability to fly between Z-levels. Carinns can fly short distances using stamina. Hoverboards that let anyone fly using the vehicle's energy. Be careful flying beyond the perimeter of the floating island, and watch your battery!

ce-roadmap-general-weather-name = Weather Effects
ce-roadmap-general-weather-desc = Dynamic weather that affects gameplay. Rain waters the garden beds and fills water collectors, while blizzards cover roads and roofs with snow, leaving snowdrifts.

ce-roadmap-antagonists-thief-name = Thief
ce-roadmap-antagonists-thief-desc = A minor antagonist interested in stealing various valuable unique items from other players. By creating their thief's hideout, they gain new abilities based on the number of stolen items.

ce-roadmap-engineering-automation-name = Floating Island Technicians
ce-roadmap-engineering-automation-desc = A department of game roles responsible for maintaining the infrastructure of the floating city, automating energy and material production using conveyor belts and various devices.

ce-roadmap-general-trade-with-empire-name = Trade with the Empire
ce-roadmap-general-trade-with-empire-desc = Trading mechanisms operating on spatial teleportation of objects - an easy way to trade with the outside world. Each player can buy goods from various factions. Each faction has its own trade terminal where you can see the available assortment and special orders that the faction needs. Completing orders can earn you a lot of money.

ce-roadmap-guard-guard-department-name = Guard Department
ce-roadmap-guard-guard-department-desc = A separate building and layer of roles focused on enforcing imperial laws, finding and neutralizing criminals, and certainly not vigilantism.

ce-roadmap-antagonists-lurker-name = Lurker
ce-roadmap-antagonists-lurker-desc = A minor antagonist that brings terror and horror to the inhabitants of the floating island. Hiding in the shadows and catching lone victims, they perform a dark ritual...

ce-roadmap-general-personal-real-estate-name = Personal Real Estate
ce-roadmap-general-personal-real-estate-desc = Personal homes, small shops, or even cafes - optional roleplay opportunities for ordinary citizens, filling the city with interesting buildings.

ce-roadmap-medical-alchemy-name = Alchemy
ce-roadmap-medical-alchemy-desc = Use rare herbs, mushrooms, or more unique ingredients to create potions with various effects that will help you in any endeavor. From simple but deadly poisons to coat your blades with, or healing remedies, to explosive alchemical bombs.

ce-roadmap-general-random-game-events-name = Random Game Events
ce-roadmap-general-random-game-events-desc = Each game day random events will occur, from useful ones like rain watering gardens, to dangerous ones like attacks by predatory harpies.

ce-roadmap-medical-hospital-name = Hospital
ce-roadmap-medical-hospital-desc = A building and an entire faction of roles dedicated to healing wounds and injuries.

ce-roadmap-guard-magic-vision-name = Magic Vision
ce-roadmap-guard-magic-vision-desc = Various actions can leave traces in the information field - and beings with magic vision (or using a special device) can track who, when, and where performed these actions. Magic traces fade over time and dissolve into space, and the new "Interrogator" role among the guard specializes in investigating crimes relying in part on magic vision.

ce-roadmap-adventures-expeditions-name = Expeditions and Mercenaries
ce-roadmap-adventures-expeditions-desc = A separate guild building and an entire layer of roles related to extracting resources from the surrounding world. A cargo single-seat flying vehicle that miners use to fly through fragments of destroyed floating islands in search of valuable resources, encountering dangerous flora and fauna in the process.

ce-roadmap-engineering-building-collapse-name = Building Collapse
ce-roadmap-engineering-building-collapse-desc = Floating islands have a natural core that keeps them in the air. Resources can be extracted from these cores, which are necessary for expanding the island, as bridges leading into the void or mines without sufficient support will collapse, potentially causing injuries.

ce-roadmap-engineering-fire-spread-name = Fire Spread
ce-roadmap-engineering-fire-spread-desc = Careless use of certain mechanisms, or deliberate sabotage by antagonists can lead to fires. A fire system capable of consuming wooden structures, buildings, and tiles. Together with tile burning, this can lead to massive building collapses.
